---
import { TRADING_NAME } from '../config/business';
import { SITE_STATE } from '../config/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Vorschau">
  <main>
    <h1>{TRADING_NAME}</h1>

    <p>
      Diese Seite ist der <strong>Neubau</strong> der Website und noch nicht fertig. Die
      Studio-Website erreichen Sie weiterhin unter <a
        href="https://iris-sunshine-oase.de">iris-sunshine-oase.de</a>.
    </p>

    {/*
      Deliberately no address, telephone number, opening hours or prices. Those are facts about a
      real business, they have exactly one authority each, and the pages that carry them are built
      in Phase 3 once ADR 0003 has given them a typed home. A holding page is not a reason to make
      a second copy — an empty field is recoverable, a wrong price is not (`CLAUDE.md`).
    */}

    <p class="state">
      Build-Status: <code>{SITE_STATE}</code>
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /*
    Still a holding page — the design from ADR 0004's draft arrives with the homepage itself. What
    changed here is only that the two values it did carry now come from the token layer, so this file
    stops being the one place on the site with numbers of its own.
  */
  main {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .state {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    /* A muted token rather than `opacity`, because opacity would also fade the colour out of the
       contrast the check guarantees — 4.56:1 at 70% opacity is not 4.56:1. */
    color: var(--colour-text-muted);
  }
</style>
